Why: GCC >= 4.7 removed -mno-cygwin.  treecc's configure.in forces
CC="gcc -mno-cygwin" for *-*-mingw* hosts (a 2000s Cygwin-hosted MinGW idiom),
so configure dies with 'C compiler cannot create executables'.  Restrict it to
Cygwin hosts; a native MinGW host just uses $CC.  New patch (not in Guix: Guix
never builds for Windows).  Requires autoreconf afterwards.

--- a/configure.in	2007-03-02 20:09:09.000000000 +0100
+++ b/configure.in	2026-10-08 00:05:06.776627395 +0200
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 dnl Turn off the cygwin library if building for Win32.
 AC_MSG_CHECKING([if building for some Win32 platform])
 case "$host" in
-	*-*-mingw*|*-*-cygwin*)
+	*-*-cygwin*)
 		platform_win32=yes
 		CC="gcc -mno-cygwin"
 		;;
